# What gets uploaded to Vercel. The site serves exactly two things: the page and
# the functions — plus the package those functions import. Everything else here is
# dev-only, and without this file the whole repo root is published as static files
# (dev.py, the test suite, the parsers, the screenshots) because Vercel serves the
# project directory as-is.
#
# This is the same allowlist rule dev.py enforces locally, so what you check in
# the emulator is what the deployment actually exposes.
tests/
scripts/
docs/
dev.py
requirements-dev.txt
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
.vercel/
